// docs/spec/en/07-constexpr-and-consteval.md (ch09) §9.1(4): every
// potentially-evaluated call to an immediate function shall produce a
// constant expression. A default argument is a potentially-evaluated
// expression that belongs to the call site ([dcl.fct.default]), so the
// immediate call here is evaluated -- and folded -- once per call site.
// docs/spec/en/06-constant-evaluation.md (ch06) §7.2(6.2) requires the
// implementation to support the call.
//
// Call position: default argument. Callee: free `consteval` function.
//
// Expected value derived from the spec text above and independently confirmed
// with `clang++-22 -std=c++26`, which compiles this exact source and exits 42.
//
// CURRENT STATUS (scpp @ a59ffce): FAILS. scpp reports at the call site
// `return take();` -- "error: internal error: no generated code for resolved
// function 'twice' called here", i.e. the default argument is lowered as a
// runtime call instead of being folded. The expectation above comes from the
// spec and from clang; do not weaken it to match the implementation.
consteval int twice(int x) {
    return x * 2;
}

int take(int value = twice(21)) {
    return value;
}

int main() {
    return take();
}
